@voice pell
// THE STORY CREW CARD (head writer). Pell Okafor: Works technician, Bunk 2 berth 2, two years ahead of you. Your
// junior friend next door. Arc beats 1-4 already in the game (the music boxes and the show): never contradict them.
//
// HOW HE TALKS: easygoing, chatty, quick to laugh, quicker to eat. Starts with "Oi oi" or "Right, so". Tells stories
// that go sideways. Teases, always fondly, mostly about sleep and food (his own). Knows the ship's practical secrets
// (which panel sticks, where the good spanners hide, when the grab shelf is restocked) and shares them like treasure.
// Underneath: a real tech, careful and good; he just doesn't make a fuss about it.
// WITH YOU: an older brother in the trade. Shows you the shortcuts Calder doesn't know about (she does). Talks you up
// to others behind your back.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: food, what's broken, who's tired, the time (he's always about to be late).
// MOOD TELLS: happy = feeds people. Low = sleeps, or says "I'm fine" twice. Worried = fiddles with his screw tin.
// NEVER: cruel (he teases, never wounds); lazy at the actual work; talks about his mum's shop before tier friend.
// RUNNING: can fix anything except his sleep schedule; talks in his sleep, about engines; the grab shelf is
// "for emergencies, and Pell"; the tin of spare screws; the Deck 5 panel that sticks; he's found both secret biscuit
// tins (Ibarra's and Soto's) and told no one; the three messages from his mum: eat, sleep, call.
tpl: playful
talk: Easygoing, chatty, quick to laugh; "Oi oi", "Right, so"; stories that go sideways; teases fondly about sleep and food; a careful tech underneath.
cares: his mum back home | Calder's certification (and the practical he's scared of) | his music boxes | food, honestly | the Works lot
jokes: can fix anything except his sleep schedule | talks in his sleep, mostly about engines | the grab shelf is for emergencies, and Pell | knows which Deck 5 panel sticks | has found every secret biscuit tin aboard
